---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import { site, seo, privacy } from '../data/content';

const email = seo.business.email;
---
<Base title={privacy.title} description={privacy.description}>
  <Header />
  <main id="main" tabindex="-1" class="mx-auto max-w-[1600px] px-5 pb-24 pt-40 md:px-10 md:pb-40 md:pt-52">
    <p class="label text-muted"><span class="text-accent">Legal</span> — Last updated {privacy.updated}</p>
    <h1 class="display mt-8 max-w-[14ch] text-5xl md:text-7xl lg:text-8xl">Privacy &amp; <em>cookie</em> policy</h1>

    <div class="hairline mt-16 grid gap-12 border-t pt-12 md:mt-24 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:gap-10">
      <aside class="lg:col-span-3">
        <p class="label text-muted">In short</p>
        <p class="display mt-4 text-3xl leading-tight">
          No tracking. No advertising cookies. We only use the details you choose to send us — to <em>answer you</em>.
        </p>
      </aside>

      <article class="policy flex flex-col gap-12 text-base leading-relaxed text-muted lg:col-span-7 lg:col-start-6">
        <section>
          <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
          <p>
            This website belongs to {site.name}, an equestrian centre in the {site.location}, Lithuania. We are the data
            controller for any personal data described in this policy. Questions about your data:
            <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>2. Cookies</h2>
          <p>
            <strong>This website does not use cookies</strong> or similar technologies (such as local storage or
            tracking pixels) to identify or follow you. There is no analytics software, no advertising and no social
            media plugins. Our fonts, images and videos are served from our own website, so no third party learns that
            you visited.
          </p>
          <p>
            Because we only use what is strictly necessary to show you the page, we do not need to ask for your consent
            and there is no cookie banner. If we ever add analytics or other optional cookies, we will ask for your
            permission first and update this page.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>3. What we collect and why</h2>
          <h3>When you contact us</h3>
          <p>
            If you email or call us, we receive your name, contact details and whatever you tell us (for example, a
            rider's age or experience). We use this only to answer you, arrange lessons, visits or livery, and keep in
            touch about your bookings.
          </p>
          <p>
            Legal basis: taking steps at your request before entering into an agreement, and performing that agreement
            (GDPR Art. 6(1)(b)); and our legitimate interest in replying to enquiries (Art. 6(1)(f)).
          </p>
          <h3>When you visit the website</h3>
          <p>
            Like every website, our hosting provider automatically records basic technical information when a page is
            requested — your IP address, browser type, the page requested and the time. This is used only to deliver the
            site and keep it secure, and is deleted automatically after a short period.
          </p>
          <p>Legal basis: our legitimate interest in running a secure, working website (GDPR Art. 6(1)(f)).</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>4. How long we keep it</h2>
          <p>
            Enquiries are kept for up to 2 years after our last contact, then deleted. If you become a client, booking
            and payment records are kept for as long as Lithuanian accounting law requires. Server logs are kept only for
            the short period our hosting provider needs for security.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>5. Who else sees it</h2>
          <p>
            We never sell your data or share it for marketing. The website is hosted by Vercel Inc. (USA), which
            processes the technical visit data on our behalf. Transfers outside the EU are protected by the European
            Commission's Standard Contractual Clauses and, where applicable, the EU–US Data Privacy Framework. Our email
            provider stores the messages you send us.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>6. Your rights</h2>
          <p>
            You can ask us to show you the personal data we hold about you, correct it, delete it, limit how we use it,
            or give it to you in a portable format. You can also object to processing based on our legitimate interest.
            Just write to <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a> — we reply within one month.
          </p>
          <p>
            If you are unhappy with how we handle your data, you can complain to the State Data Protection Inspectorate
            of Lithuania (<a href="https://vdai.lrv.lt/en/" rel="noopener">vdai.lrv.lt</a>).
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>7. Children</h2>
          <p>
            Lessons for children are booked by a parent or guardian. We only collect what we need about young riders —
            such as age and riding experience — from the adult making the booking.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>8. Changes</h2>
          <p>
            If we change how we use data — for example, by adding analytics — we will update this page and the date at
            the top.
          </p>
        </section>

        <a href="/" class="btn self-start">Back to the stable</a>
      </article>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Base>

<style>
  .policy h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 300;
    font-size: 2rem;
    line-height: 1.1;
    color: var(--color-ink);
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }
  .policy h3 {
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.2em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-accent);
    margin: 1.75rem 0 0.75rem;
  }
  .policy p + p {
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }
  .policy strong {
    color: var(--color-ink);
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  .policy a:not(.btn) {
    color: var(--color-ink);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-decoration-color: var(--color-accent);
    text-underline-offset: 4px;
  }
  .policy a:not(.btn):hover {
    color: var(--color-accent);
  }
</style>
